Z||000000||LZeitgeist||09-08-2001||08:37 AM||||Got a Pontiac car show there today (Saturday 9/8) hosted by the local GTO club - got trophies for GTO-types and Firebird-types, and decade award trophies... dash plaques to the first 100 registered...<P>Registration from 9am - noon - $15<P>Judging from 12:30 - 2:30, trophies handed out at 3:00...<P><BR>Wen I register, I'm going to ask if they're a 'Fiero-friendly' crowd... hopefully so... it'd be cool to have some more Pontiac friends in the area. <P>Hopefully my car (and others) can project a little respect and camaraderie for our beloved little P-body.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Patrick W. Heinske  --  LZeitgeist@aol.com<BR>1988 Red Fiero Formula<BR>- 1st Place - Stock Coupe - FOCOSEVA 2000<BR>- 3rd Place - Stock Formula - FOCOA Nat'l 2001<p>[This message has been edited by LZeitgeist (edited 09-08-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula88||09-08-2001||06:30 PM||||I guess you could say they were Fiero friendly.  Pat won a plaque in his class, 82-present Pontiac.  He was competing against the likes of 2002 Firehawks, 20th Anniversary T/A's and a bunch of 90's F-bodies.  BTW, Pat's was the ONLY Fiero there!  There was an 87 GT, but it left before judging ended.  I didn't enter my beast, cuz she was no where near ready.  <P>My favorite was the 71 Lucerne Blue Trans Am.  Yum Yum!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Formula88 (edited 09-08-2001).]||||reg||1
